{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (NURSE): Got his vitals and the urine dip done before you came in. Dip shows large blood, three plus, leukocytes negative, nitrites negative. Blood pressure one forty eight over ninety two, pulse ninety six, temp thirty six point nine celsius, sats ninety eight percent, respirations eighteen.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (DOCTOR): Umm. Sorry, hold on, this screen is frozen again. What was that pressure?",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (NURSE): One forty eight over ninety two. My sister passed a kidney stone last spring, up all night, so this looked real familiar to me.",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (DOCTOR): Right. Sir, what brought you in today?",
  "[SEG0005] person_3 (PATIENT): Side.",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (DOCTOR): Side. Which side? Say it again, I was clicking.",
  "[SEG0007] person_3 (PATIENT): Left.",
  "[SEG0008] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): It started around two in the morning, left side, really sharp, shooting down into his groin. He was pacing the hallway and he couldn't—",
  "[SEG0009] person_2 (DOCTOR): Sorry, couldn't what? The computer just beeped at me.",
  "[SEG0010] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Couldn't stay still. And the pain, he kept grabbing his side.",
  "[SEG0011] person_2 (DOCTOR): How bad is it, zero to ten?",
  "[SEG0012] person_3 (PATIENT): Eight. Maybe.",
  "[SEG0013] person_2 (DOCTOR): Eight, maybe. Okay. Did you vomit?",
  "[SEG0014] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): He threw up once, in the bathroom, just bile, and that was it, and then there was blood in the toilet when he peed.",
  "[SEG0015] person_2 (DOCTOR): You saw blood?",
  "[SEG0016] person_3 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0017] person_2 (DOCTOR): Any fever overnight?",
  "[SEG0018] person_3 (PATIENT): Groin.",
  "[SEG0019] person_2 (DOCTOR): No, not the groin. Fever. Did you feel hot, or chilled?",
  "[SEG0020] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0021] person_2 (DOCTOR): Burning when you pee?",
  "[SEG0022] person_3 (PATIENT): Never.",
  "[SEG0023] person_2 (DOCTOR): Are you nauseous sitting here?",
  "[SEG0024] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0025] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): He's had high blood pressure for years. Takes lysinopril.",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (DOCTOR): Lysinopril. Dose? The med list didn't load, say it again.",
  "[SEG0027] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Twenty milligrams every morning, by mouth.",
  "[SEG0028] person_3 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0029] person_2 (DOCTOR): Any chest pain tonight, or with the blood pressure?",
  "[SEG0030] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0031] person_2 (DOCTOR): Shortness of breath?",
  "[SEG0032] person_3 (PATIENT): Not really.",
  "[SEG0033] person_2 (DOCTOR): Headaches? From the pressure, I mean.",
  "[SEG0034] person_3 (PATIENT): No. Well, sometimes.",
  "[SEG0035] person_2 (DOCTOR): Sometimes. For how long have those been going on?",
  "[SEG0036] person_3 (PATIENT): Years.",
  "[SEG0037] person_2 (DOCTOR): Diarrhea at all?",
  "[SEG0038] person_3 (PATIENT): Not that either.",
  "[SEG0039] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): He doesn't smoke, never has. He had two beers at the game yesterday, which isn't really like him, he barely—",
  "[SEG0040] person_2 (DOCTOR): Hold on. Two beers, you said? I only caught half.",
  "[SEG0041] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Two beers yesterday. He barely drinks.",
  "[SEG0042] person_2 (DOCTOR): Alright. I think there's a stone in the ureter. That little tube spasms trying to push it along, and that's why the pain runs from the loin down to the groin. The dip had no white cells, so I'm not calling this an infection.",
  "[SEG0043] person_2 (DOCTOR): I'm ordering a noncontrast CT of the abdomen and pelvis today, and ketorolac ten milligrams by mouth, one dose now, for the pain.",
  "[SEG0044] person_1 (NURSE): CT slot is at 2 this afternoon, I'll book it. I can hand him the ketorolac as soon as it's signed.",
  "[SEG0045] person_2 (DOCTOR): Good. Come back to clinic tomorrow morning and we'll go over it. If the pain gets worse before then, come straight back in. Drink water today, not beer.",
  "[SEG0046] person_3 (PATIENT): Okay."
 ],
